.\" Man page for whiskerless. Debian policy expects one for anything in
.\" /usr/bin, and lintian flags its absence — which matters now that the
.\" packages go into a repository rather than only onto a release page.
.\"
.\" A repo invariant (tests/test_repo_invariants.py) asserts every CLI
.\" subcommand appears here, so the two cannot drift silently.
.TH WHISKERLESS 1 "2026-08-17" "whiskerless" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
whiskerless \- fully-local MQTT control for the Whisker Litter-Robot 4
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B whiskerless
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B whiskerless
re-points a Whisker Litter\-Robot 4 away from Whisker's cloud and onto an MQTT
broker you control, then reads its telemetry and changes its settings over that
broker. The robot keeps its firmware; nothing is opened, soldered or reflashed,
and re-onboarding it in the Whisker app puts it back.
.PP
The robot cannot send a username or a password \(em its firmware has no field
for one, because it was built for AWS IoT, which authenticates clients by
certificate. Certificates are therefore the only authentication available, and
.B whiskerless
runs a small certificate authority on your behalf to provide them.
.SH SETUP COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup
Prepare this machine: the broker it talks to, and the certificates for it.
Offers to create a certificate authority, issues your broker's server
certificate and this machine's own identity, and prints the three files to
install on the broker. Run once, before any robot.
.TP
.B provision
Re-provision a robot onto your broker over Bluetooth. Prompts for the serial,
lists the networks the robot can see, and writes your CA, an identity for the
robot, and your broker's address into its flash. Refuses on a machine that has
not been through
.BR setup .
.TP
.B backup " [\fIpath\fR]"
Save this machine's setup \(em the certificate authority, the broker and every
robot profile \(em to one file. Offers to encrypt it. The CA private key is the
only thing here that cannot be regenerated.
.TP
.B restore " \fIfile\fR"
Put a backup back. Refuses to replace an existing setup without
.BR \-\-force ,
and names the robots that would stop trusting your broker if it did.
.SH EVERYDAY COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
The derived view: what this robot is doing, in plain terms.
.TP
.B state
Request and decode the full state document.
.TP
.B monitor
Watch state and activity as they arrive. Read\-only.
.TP
.B set " \fIname\fR \fIvalue\fR"
Change a setting. Writes, then reads back to confirm it committed.
.TP
.B calibrate " full|empty"
Record what a full (or empty) globe looks like on this robot, so the litter
percentage means something.
.SH PANEL COMMANDS
These emit the same code the physical panel does, so the firmware's pinch,
cat\-detect and bonnet interlocks apply exactly as they do to a finger.
.TP
.B clean-cycle
Run a clean cycle. Turns the globe.
.TP
.B panel-reset
Press Reset \(em acknowledge a full\-drawer alarm, or release a stalled cycle.
.TP
.B empty-cycle
Empty the globe into the waste drawer. Costs a litter refill.
.TP
.B wifi-toggle
Toggle the robot's WiFi. It may not come back: a robot with WiFi off has left
the network, and only a physical press returns it.
.TP
.B power
Toggle robot power. Same warning \(em nothing over MQTT can undo it.
.SH SAVED ROBOTS
.TP
.B robots
List the robots set up on this machine. Damaged profiles are shown as such.
.TP
.B use " \fIserial\fR"
Choose which robot the bare commands act on.
.TP
.B forget " \fIserial\fR"
Remove a robot's saved details from this machine. The robot keeps running.
.SH PROTOCOL COMMANDS
.TP
.B read " \fIregister\fR"
Type\-1 read of a register.
.TP
.B send " \fIcode\fR"
Send a raw
.I 0xTTRRVVVV
code. Passes through the safety guard, which refuses brick and reset\-class
opcodes unconditionally \(em there is no override flag.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase logging;
.B \-vv
for debug.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Show the full traceback on failure, for bug reports.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/whiskerless/
Everything this machine knows: the certificate authority, the one broker it
talks to, this machine's client identity, and one directory per robot. Deliberately
not hidden, because it holds a key you are told to back up.
.TP
.I ~/whiskerless/ca/ca.key
The private key that signs certificates for your robots. Losing it does not stop
robots that already work; it costs you the ability to add or re\-provision one
without visiting every robot you own.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WHISKERLESS_HOME
Use a different store. A genuinely separate broker is a separate store.
.TP
.B WHISKERLESS_BACKUP_PASSWORD
Passphrase for
.B backup
and
.BR restore ,
for unattended use.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An error, reported as one line rather than a traceback.
.TP
.B 2
Refused by the safety guard.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation, the protocol reference and the Home Assistant integration:
.UR https://github.com/SisyphusMD/whiskerless
.UE
.SH AUTHOR
Whiskerless <whiskerless@bryantserver.com>
